Better default tolerances for method of snapshots?
See discussion in #1012.

@lbalicki, as I understand https://www.netlib.org/lapack/lug/node89.html, then every EV smaller than the largest eigenvalue times machine precision should be considered as potentially zero. Everything else should be guaranteed to be a non-zero EV. So maybe it would make sense to throw everything away below that threshold (or a fixed constant times this threshold) and trust that the corresponding eigenvectors are at least not linearly dependent?

